<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Spells</h1>
<p>Spells are divided into categories called spheres. Your ability in a sphere 
decides both how well you cast its spells, and how well you resist a similar 
spell cast on you: as far as your ability goes, it protects you as well.
</p><p>These are the spheres, each with its own help:
</p>
<pre><a cmd='#'>help divine sphere</a>, <a cmd='#'>help protection sphere</a>, <a cmd='#'>help detection sphere</a>,
<a cmd='#'>help summoning sphere</a>, <a cmd='#'>help creation sphere</a>, <a cmd='#'>help mind sphere</a>,
<a cmd='#'>help fire sphere</a>, <a cmd='#'>help frost sphere</a>, <a cmd='#'>help electricity sphere</a>,
<a cmd='#'>help poison sphere</a>, <a cmd='#'>help acid sphere</a>
</pre>
<p>To cast a spell, see <a cmd='#'>Help Casting</a>. Which spells your guild teaches you is in 
the list for your guild, for example <a cmd='#'>help healer spells</a> or 
<a cmd='#'>help conjurer spells</a>, and each spell has its own help: help and the name.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Casting</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Skills</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Practice</a>
</pre>




</div>